#descr "The Dragonkin of Faerûn, not to be confused with the more intelligent Dragonborn native to Abeir, are believed to be the distant cousins of chromatic dragons. They formed wild tribes around Toril and were often enthralled into the service of powerful and malevolent humans, especially by members of the Cult of the Dragon.

These draconic beasts stood much taller than other humanoids, with scaled hides ranging in color from ocher to reddish-brown. Their gray-green wings were fully functional. In combat, they preferred to engage their enemies from the air, driving down and striking with their claws and weapons and following up with their fiery breath weapon.  

During the 13th century DR, a tribe of dragonkin resided in the mountains overlooking the Bottomless Bogs in Vaasa. Recruited and trained by the Cult of the Draogn, they joined the Wearers of Purple in their quest to corrupt the Mythal in Myth Drannor and taint the Pool of Radiance underneath Castle Cormanthor." 
